+## Platform-call failure policy
+
+- First failure: retry the exact same tool and arguments once after a short backoff.
+- If either failure indicates an MCP session problem: discard the cached session, initialize a new one, and retry once more.
+- HTTP 401: do not retry or refresh; report `credential_problem` and leave the API key unchanged.
+- HTTP 429: back off and retry once without increasing concurrency.
+- `can't start new thread`: treat as an upstream transient/backend error and apply only the bounded retry above.
+- When retries are exhausted, the CLI reports `layer=TikHub` and `status=unavailable`. Web Search or Jina may be offered only as explicitly labeled `secondary evidence`; their output is never TikHub/platform-ground-truth data.
+
